    region photo-intro (
        name: Explore your photos
        type: staticContent
        source {
            htmlCode:
                ```html
                <section class="photo-hero" aria-labelledby="photo-hero-title">
                  <div class="photo-hero__eyebrow">Oracle APEX · MLE · WebAssembly</div>
                  <h2 id="photo-hero-title">Explore the story behind your photos</h2>
                  <p>Upload a photo to explore its metadata and see Oracle APEX, JavaScript and WebAssembly work together in the database. A thumbnail is generated in the background; JPEG uploads also get an Error Level Analysis (ELA) image. Choose JPEG for the full demonstration.</p>
                </section>
                ```
        }
        layout {
            sequence: 20
            slot: body
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/buttons-container
            templateOptions: [
                #DEFAULT#
                margin-bottom-md
                t-ButtonRegion--noPadding
                t-ButtonRegion--noUI
            ]
        }
        advanced {
            htmlDomId: photo-intro
        }
    )

    region about (
        name: About
        type: staticContent
        source {
            htmlCode:
                ```html
                This application demonstrates many out-of-the-box features of APEX while also showing how an APEX developer can enhance and extend functionality with some custom HTML, mininmal CSS and some Javascript. Further, this application should behave beautifully on either Desktop or Mobile devices!
                <h3>App Development concepts</h3>
                <ul>
                <li>Single Page Application</li>
                <li>Progressive Web App</li>
                <li>Mobile Friendly - can use device location and camera</li>
                <li>File upload</li>
                <li>Activity locations map</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Database & APEX concepts</h3>
                <ul>
                <li>Page Designer</li>
                <li>QuickSQL and relational datamodel</li>
                <li>Form Region</li>
                <li>Cards Region</li>
                <li>Dialogs</li>
                <li>Working with BLOBs</li>
                <li>Javascript</li>
                <li>Dynamic Actions</li>
                <li>Custom Events</li>
                <li>Custom HTML and CSS styling</li>
                </ul>
                ```
        }
        layout {
            sequence: 40
            slot: dialogsDrawersAndPopups
        }
        appearance {
            template: @/inline-drawer
            templateOptions: [
                #DEFAULT#
                js-dialog-class-t-Drawer--pullOutEnd
            ]
        }
        advanced {
            htmlDomId: about
            regionDisplaySelector: true
        }
    )

